# Self-Testing Checklist — Mandatory Before Completion

After completing any non-trivial task (feature, bug fix, refactor), execute this checklist BEFORE presenting the result. DO NOT skip any section.

## Severity & Confidence Rules

- Classify every finding as **P0** (Critical) / **P1** (High) / **P2** (Medium) / **P3** (Low)
- Only report findings with **>80% confidence** of being a real issue
- Borderline findings (60-80%) → flag as **Question** for the reviewer
- Use **Issue → Suggestion → Why** format for every finding

## 1. Code Quality

- [ ] No function > 40 lines without justification
- [ ] No duplicated logic — shared code extracted
- [ ] Error cases handled with try/catch or error boundaries
- [ ] Semantic naming (no `tmp`, `data1`, `doStuff`)

## 2. Design & Complexity (skip if trivial config/docs change)

- [ ] Code is not more complex than necessary (no over-engineering, no speculative features)
- [ ] "Clever" code does not sacrifice readability for brevity
- [ ] A future developer can easily understand and modify this code
- [ ] **SRP**: Each changed class/module has a single reason to change
- [ ] **OCP**: Behavior extended via abstraction, not by modifying stable code
- [ ] **DIP**: High-level modules depend on abstractions, not concrete implementations
- [ ] No god functions, no feature envy, no shotgun surgery
- [ ] Import hierarchy respected: shared → (components | core) → kit-bg → kit → apps (kit-bg NEVER imports components)

## 3. React Check (skip if no component code touched)

- [ ] No inline `?? []` / `?? {}` in render — use module-level constants or `useMemo`
- [ ] No new object/array creation in render paths feeding dependency arrays
- [ ] All `useMemo`/`useCallback` dependency arrays correct
- [ ] No unstable props passed to memoized children
- [ ] State not lifted unnecessarily high causing wide re-render fanout

## 4. Cross-Platform Impact (skip if single-platform file)

- [ ] Identified which platforms consume modified code
- [ ] UI changes verified on mobile (narrowest) and desktop (widest)
- [ ] Stated: "Affects: [platforms]" and "Does NOT affect: [platforms]"

## 5. Business Logic & Regression

- [ ] Implementation matches original requirement
- [ ] Edge cases covered: empty data, null, loading, error states
- [ ] Data flow end-to-end: API → state → UI
- [ ] Shared hook/utility modified → checked all consumers
- [ ] Type definitions changed → all consumers updated
- [ ] State atoms modified → verified all readers/writers

## 6. Security Scan (skip for pure UI styling with no data handling)

Adopt 3-phase methodology: **context → compare → assess**

- [ ] No sensitive data in logs/telemetry/error reports (mnemonics, private keys, API keys, PII)
- [ ] Auth guards wrap every protected route and cannot be bypassed
- [ ] No new eval/dynamic execution/unsafe deserialization introduced
- [ ] Crypto operations follow established patterns (no weak algorithms, no hardcoded keys)
- [ ] Input validation present for all external/user inputs
- [ ] Only flag issues with >80% confidence of real exploitation potential

## 7. Potential Bugs (skip for docs/config-only changes)

- [ ] No race conditions in async operations
- [ ] No stale closures capturing outdated state
- [ ] No memory leaks: subscriptions/listeners cleaned up
- [ ] No infinite loops from useEffect dependency chains
- [ ] "Not loaded" (`null`/`undefined`) vs "empty" (`[]`) properly distinguished
- [ ] Boundary conditions: off-by-one, integer overflow, null coalescing

## 8. Removal Candidates

- [ ] No dead code left behind (unused functions/components/exports after this change)
- [ ] No redundant code that should be extracted into shared utility
- [ ] No stale feature flags that should be cleaned up
- [ ] No new TODO/FIXME without a tracking issue

## 9. Tests (skip for pure UI styling with no logic)

Review tests with the same rigor as production code:

- [ ] New/modified logic has corresponding `.test.ts` file
- [ ] Tests cover happy path AND edge cases (empty, null, error)
- [ ] Tests will actually fail if the code breaks (no tautological assertions)
- [ ] Bug fix includes a regression test
- [ ] Tests pass: `yarn test -- --testPathPattern=<path>`

## 10. Lint & Type Check

- [ ] `ReadLints` shows no new errors on modified files
- [ ] `yarn lint:staged` passes
- [ ] `yarn tsc:staged` passes

## 11. Manual Verification (skip for non-UI changes)

- Which command to run (`yarn app:ios` / `yarn app:desktop` / `yarn app:web` / `yarn app:ext`)
- Which page to open and what action to perform
- What the expected behavior is
- Edge cases to check: empty state, error state, loading state

## 12. Summary Output

Present to user using **Issue → Suggestion → Why** format for all findings:

```markdown
## Review Summary

**What was done**: 1-2 sentences
**Files modified/created**: list
**Tests added/updated**: list

### Findings (if any)

**Finding N**: `path/to/file.ts:LXX` [P0/P1/P2/P3] (XX% confidence)
- **Issue**: What is wrong
- **Suggestion**: Concrete fix (with code snippet if applicable)
- **Why**: Explanation of the risk/impact

### Impact
- **Affects**: [platforms]
- **Does NOT affect**: [platforms]
- **Risk assessment**: Low / Medium / High / Critical

### Self-test result
- Which checks passed
- Which were skipped and why
- Remaining questions or concerns
```

## Bug Fix Case Recording

After every **bug fix**, append to `.claude/skills/1k-retrospective/references/case-studies.md`:

```
## Case: [Title]
**Date**: YYYY-MM-DD | **Platforms**: [affected]
**Symptom**: [what the user saw]
**Root Cause**: [what was actually wrong]
**Fix**: [what was changed]
**Catchable by**: [Section N: check item, or "NEW — not covered"]
```

Do NOT modify this file directly — only append to `case-studies.md`.

## Skip Rules

- Sections 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8, 11: see "skip if" notes in each section header
- NEVER skip Sections 1, 5, 10, and 12
